/// The platform's module: answers, to `build`, the platform the
/// host hands every program, whose members are the program's standard
/// output, the collections, the kernel classes a program may name, a
/// stopwatch, the typed arrays and the mirrors. The host instantiates it
/// once, at boot.
///
/// The module behind the platform a module is handed (§8.3): a shipped
/// core-library module, booted by the host with the VM mirror and the
/// kernel instance (`docs/design/core-library.md`, "The module table and
/// the boot").
///
/// The factory pattern: this root holds what is privileged -- the mirror,
/// the kernel instance, which it builds the collections, typed arrays and
/// mirrors modules over, and the kernel's classes `KernelNamespace` hands
/// out --
/// and the host never hands its instance to anyone. It
/// instantiates the root once, sends it `build`, its one public member, and
/// hands every program that platform, an instance of the nested class
/// `Platform`, whose factory is a harmless `new`. What a program receives
/// are instances of the nested classes, the facets, through the platform's
/// members; each reaches the mirror and the kernel's classes lexically, as
/// a member of this root, never through a slot of its own, so every one of
/// them writes through the one mirror. The nested classes are private, so
/// even a holder of this root's instance could send it nothing but `build`:
/// a second line of defence behind the instance being unreachable. The
/// transcript, the clock, the collections, the typed arrays and the
/// mirrors are each a module of their own, another such root
/// (`platform/TranscriptFactory.ns`, `platform/TimeFactory.ns`,
/// `platform/CollectionsFactory.ns`, `platform/TypedArraysFactory.ns`,
/// `platform/MirrorsFactory.ns`), whose one instance this root builds
/// through the mirror on its first use and keeps in a private lazy slot
/// here; the platform hands out only the facets their `build` answers.
/// Nothing a program can name answers this root's instance or its class,
/// so no program can build a second one over something that is not the
/// mirror. Keep it so: no code whose receiver is
/// this root's instance may send it anything it does not understand, since
/// a `MessageNotUnderstood` hands its receiver to whoever catches it
/// (`docs/design/core-library.md`, "No program reaches a shipped module's
/// root"). For the same reason neither the mirror nor the kernel instance
/// is ever an argument of a send to a receiver that may not understand
/// it: a `MessageNotUnderstood` hands its message's arguments to whoever
/// catches it too.
///
/// The factory's parameters are copied into slots because neither a lazy
/// slot nor a method may name them (§6); a root keeps what it uses, so of
/// the kernel it keeps the instance, which the lazy module slots build
/// over, and the classes `KernelNamespace` hands out, and nothing hands
/// the instance on but to the factories of those three modules. A
/// send to `vmMirror` here is a mirror send, as in `Kernel.ns`: this module
/// is resolved with `resolve_kernel`, which only shipped source is.
///
/// Everything here is a value (§3.1.1): stateless but for what the host
/// hands the root and the modules built on first use, which the root
/// reaches through the mirror.
///
/// @factory makes the platform's module over `mirror` and `kernel`,
/// copying the mirror into `vmMirror`, the kernel instance into
/// `kernelModule` and each kernel class `KernelNamespace` hands out into a
/// slot of its own; the host sends it once, at boot.
/// @param mirror the VM mirror, which the host alone holds.
/// @param kernel the kernel module's instance, whose classes
/// `KernelNamespace` hands out.
(* :module: newspeak.core.PlatformFactory *)
class PlatformFactory usingVmMirror: mirror kernel: kernel = Value (
  |
    /// The VM mirror the factory was given: the one object through which
    /// a member here reaches a native operation. Never handed out.
    private vmMirror = mirror.
    /// The kernel module's instance the factory was given, which the
    /// collections, typed arrays and mirrors modules are built over on
    /// first demand. Kept because those builds need the instance itself, not
    /// only its classes; handed to nothing but their factories, never to
    /// a program, and sent nothing but `garbageCollect`, which it
    /// understands.
    private kernelModule = kernel.
    /// The kernel's `Exception`, which `KernelNamespace` hands out.
    /// Read from the kernel instance once, as the factory runs; every
    /// `platform kernel` facet answers it.
    private Exception = kernel Exception.
    /// The kernel's `Error`, which `KernelNamespace` hands out.
    /// Read from the kernel instance once, as the factory runs; every
    /// `platform kernel` facet answers it.
    private Error = kernel Error.
    /// The kernel's `MessageNotUnderstood`, which `KernelNamespace` hands out.
    /// Read from the kernel instance once, as the factory runs; every
    /// `platform kernel` facet answers it.
    private MessageNotUnderstood = kernel MessageNotUnderstood.
    /// The kernel's `Halt`, which `KernelNamespace` hands out.
    /// Read from the kernel instance once, as the factory runs; every
    /// `platform kernel` facet answers it.
    private Halt = kernel Halt.
    /// The kernel's `Message`, which `KernelNamespace` hands out.
    /// Read from the kernel instance once, as the factory runs; every
    /// `platform kernel` facet answers it.
    private Message = kernel Message.
    /// The kernel's `ArgumentError`, which `KernelNamespace` hands out.
    /// Read from the kernel instance once, as the factory runs; every
    /// `platform kernel` facet answers it.
    private ArgumentError = kernel ArgumentError.
    /// The kernel's `CannotReturn`, which `KernelNamespace` hands out.
    /// Read from the kernel instance once, as the factory runs; every
    /// `platform kernel` facet answers it.
    private CannotReturn = kernel CannotReturn.
    /// The kernel's `CannotInstantiate`, which `KernelNamespace` hands out.
    /// Read from the kernel instance once, as the factory runs; every
    /// `platform kernel` facet answers it.
    private CannotInstantiate = kernel CannotInstantiate.
    /// The kernel's `Closure`, which `KernelNamespace` hands out.
    /// Read from the kernel instance once, as the factory runs; every
    /// `platform kernel` facet answers it.
    private Closure = kernel Closure.
    /// The kernel's `Future`, which `KernelNamespace` hands out.
    /// Read from the kernel instance once, as the factory runs; every
    /// `platform kernel` facet answers it.
    private Future = kernel Future.
    /// The kernel's `Proxy`, which `KernelNamespace` hands out.
    /// Read from the kernel instance once, as the factory runs; every
    /// `platform kernel` facet answers it.
    private Proxy = kernel Proxy.
    /// The kernel's `Collection`, which `KernelNamespace` hands out.
    /// Read from the kernel instance once, as the factory runs; every
    /// `platform kernel` facet answers it.
    private Collection = kernel Collection.
    /// The kernel's `StringBuilder`, which `KernelNamespace` hands out.
    /// Read from the kernel instance once, as the factory runs; every
    /// `platform kernel` facet answers it.
    private StringBuilder = kernel StringBuilder.
    /// The kernel's `DataView`, which `KernelNamespace` hands out.
    /// Read from the kernel instance once, as the factory runs; every
    /// `platform kernel` facet answers it.
    private DataView = kernel DataView.
    /// The kernel's `WeakArray`, which `KernelNamespace` hands out.
    /// Read from the kernel instance once, as the factory runs; every
    /// `platform kernel` facet answers it.
    private WeakArray = kernel WeakArray.
    /// The kernel's `Ephemeron`, which `KernelNamespace` hands out.
    /// Read from the kernel instance once, as the factory runs; every
    /// `platform kernel` facet answers it.
    private Ephemeron = kernel Ephemeron.
    /// The kernel's `WeakMap`, which `KernelNamespace` hands out.
    /// Read from the kernel instance once, as the factory runs; every
    /// `platform kernel` facet answers it.
    private WeakMap = kernel WeakMap.
  |
) (
  /// The one collections module, built over the kernel on first use and
  /// the same object on every use after it.
  ///
  /// The mirror answers a module's one instance once it is recorded, so
  /// every platform's facet comes from one factory and hands out one
  /// `List` class. Until then the mirror answers the module's root class,
  /// which is sent its factory, and records what the factory answered as
  /// that one instance. The factory goes only to a class the mirror
  /// answered; a declined lookup leaves the slot `nil` and sends nothing,
  /// so the kernel instance, and the mirror in the other modules' slots,
  /// is never the argument of a send `nil` does not understand, whose
  /// `MessageNotUnderstood` would hand it to whoever catches it. A demand
  /// an unwind interrupts -- the depth limit reached inside the factory --
  /// records nothing, so the next demand builds the module again from the
  /// same class. A record the mirror declines -- a defect in the binary --
  /// leaves the slot `nil`, so the next read demands the module again and
  /// the member that wanted it fails loudly, sending `build` to `nil`. The
  /// module's instance is as private as this one: only the facets its
  /// `build` answers leave this module.
  lazy private collectionsModule = vmMirror moduleInstanceNamed: #CollectionsFactory ifFail: [
    |
      rootClass = vmMirror shippedModuleClassNamed: #CollectionsFactory ifFail: [nil].
    |
    rootClass isNil ifFalse: [
      vmMirror recordShippedModule: (rootClass usingKernel: kernelModule) ifFail: [nil].
    ].
  ].

  /// The one transcript module, built over the mirror on first use and
  /// the same object on every use after it, as `collectionsModule` is: the
  /// factory goes only to a class the mirror answered, and a demand an
  /// unwind interrupts records nothing, so the next one builds the module
  /// again. Only the transcripts its `build` answers leave this module.
  lazy private transcriptModule = vmMirror moduleInstanceNamed: #TranscriptFactory ifFail: [
    |
      rootClass = vmMirror shippedModuleClassNamed: #TranscriptFactory ifFail: [nil].
    |
    rootClass isNil ifFalse: [
      vmMirror recordShippedModule: (rootClass usingVmMirror: vmMirror) ifFail: [nil].
    ].
  ].

  /// The one clock module, built over the mirror on first use and the
  /// same object on every use after it, as `collectionsModule` is: the
  /// factory goes only to a class the mirror answered, and a demand an
  /// unwind interrupts records nothing, so the next one builds the module
  /// again. Only the `Time` namespaces its `build` answers leave this
  /// module.
  lazy private timeModule = vmMirror moduleInstanceNamed: #TimeFactory ifFail: [
    |
      rootClass = vmMirror shippedModuleClassNamed: #TimeFactory ifFail: [nil].
    |
    rootClass isNil ifFalse: [
      vmMirror recordShippedModule: (rootClass usingVmMirror: vmMirror) ifFail: [nil].
    ].
  ].

  /// The one typed arrays module, built over the mirror and the kernel on
  /// first use and the same object on every use after it, as
  /// `collectionsModule` is: the factory goes only to a class the mirror
  /// answered, and a demand an unwind interrupts records nothing, so the
  /// next one builds the module again. Only the `TypedArrays` namespaces
  /// its `build` answers leave this module.
  lazy private typedArraysModule = vmMirror moduleInstanceNamed: #TypedArraysFactory ifFail: [
    |
      rootClass = vmMirror shippedModuleClassNamed: #TypedArraysFactory ifFail: [nil].
    |
    rootClass isNil ifFalse: [
      vmMirror recordShippedModule: (rootClass usingVmMirror: vmMirror kernel: kernelModule)
          ifFail: [nil].
    ].
  ].

  /// The one mirrors module, built over the mirror and the kernel on
  /// first use and the same object on every use after it, as
  /// `collectionsModule` is: the factory goes only to a class the mirror
  /// answered, and a demand an unwind interrupts records nothing, so the
  /// next one builds the module again. Only the `Mirrors` namespaces its
  /// `build` answers leave this module.
  lazy private mirrorsModule = vmMirror moduleInstanceNamed: #MirrorsFactory ifFail: [
    |
      rootClass = vmMirror shippedModuleClassNamed: #MirrorsFactory ifFail: [nil].
    |
    rootClass isNil ifFalse: [
      vmMirror recordShippedModule: (rootClass usingVmMirror: vmMirror kernel: kernelModule)
          ifFail: [nil].
    ].
  ].

  /// The platform a program is handed: the namespace of what it may use
  /// beyond the kernel, each member built on first use.
  ///
  /// §8.3 describes the platform as an object that "provides accessors to
  /// various modules"; each is a lazy slot (§6.3.3), built on first use,
  /// so a program pays only for what it asks for. It hands out none of
  /// this module's classes: a program holds the instances its members
  /// answer, and since `class` is protected it reaches no class of
  /// theirs, so it can make no second platform or transcript. `Time`
  /// hands out `Stopwatch`, which a program instantiates itself, the
  /// collections facet the collections module's classes, the typed
  /// arrays facet the typed arrays module's classes, and the mirrors
  /// facet the mirrors module's public classes.
  private class Platform = Value () (
    /// The program's standard output, a `Transcript`, written as UTF-8.
    /// Built on first use; every later send answers the same one.
    lazy public transcript = transcriptModule build.

    /// The namespace of the collections module's classes -- `List`,
    /// `Map`, `IdentityMap`, `Set` and the Errors `NotFound` and
    /// `ConcurrentModification` -- and of the kernel's `Collection`.
    /// Built on first use; every later send answers the same one.
    lazy public collections = collectionsModule build.

    /// The namespace of the kernel classes a program may name, a
    /// `KernelNamespace`. Built on first use; every later send answers
    /// the same one.
    lazy public kernel = KernelNamespace new.

    /// The namespace of `Stopwatch`, a `Time`. Built on first use;
    /// every later send answers the same one.
    lazy public time = timeModule build.

    /// The namespace of the typed arrays module's classes -- `TypedArray`
    /// and the ten typed arrays, `Int8Array` to `Float64Array` -- a
    /// `TypedArrays`. Built on first use; every later send answers the
    /// same one.
    ///
    /// Exempt from the rule that an accessor here exists only because a
    /// program needs it, as `kernel` is: it hands out a whole module of
    /// the core library's classes, not a piece of the platform's services.
    lazy public typedArrays = typedArraysModule build.

    /// The namespace of the mirrors module's public classes --
    /// `ObjectMirror` and `ClassMirror`, through which a program reads the
    /// structure of its objects and classes -- a `Mirrors`. Built on first
    /// use; every later send answers the same one.
    ///
    /// Exempt from the rule that an accessor here exists only because a
    /// program needs it, as `kernel` and `typedArrays` are: it hands out
    /// classes of a core-library module and reaches no host.
    lazy public mirrors = mirrorsModule build.
  )

  /// `platform kernel`: the kernel classes a program may name that
  /// `Object`'s class accessors do not answer, and `Closure`, which they
  /// answer too; and `garbageCollect`, the full collection a program
  /// asks for to see a weak slot cleared.
  ///
  /// The facet over the kernel module: it hands out the kernel's classes,
  /// never the kernel instance, which it reaches only as a member of this
  /// module's root.
  private class KernelNamespace = Value () (
    /// Hands out the kernel's `Exception` class to a program.
    ///
    /// @answers the kernel's class `Exception`, the same class on every send.
    public Exception = (
      ^outer PlatformFactory Exception.
    )

    /// Hands out the kernel's `Error` class to a program.
    ///
    /// @answers the kernel's class `Error`, the same class on every send.
    public Error = (
      ^outer PlatformFactory Error.
    )

    /// Hands out the kernel's `MessageNotUnderstood` class to a program.
    ///
    /// @answers the kernel's class `MessageNotUnderstood`, the same class on every send.
    public MessageNotUnderstood = (
      ^outer PlatformFactory MessageNotUnderstood.
    )

    /// Hands out the kernel's `Halt` class to a program.
    ///
    /// @answers the kernel's class `Halt`, the same class on every send.
    public Halt = (
      ^outer PlatformFactory Halt.
    )

    /// Hands out the kernel's `Message` class to a program.
    ///
    /// @answers the kernel's class `Message`, the same class on every send.
    public Message = (
      ^outer PlatformFactory Message.
    )

    /// Hands out the kernel's `ArgumentError` class to a program.
    ///
    /// @answers the kernel's class `ArgumentError`, the same class on every send.
    public ArgumentError = (
      ^outer PlatformFactory ArgumentError.
    )

    /// Hands out the kernel's `CannotReturn` class to a program.
    ///
    /// @answers the kernel's class `CannotReturn`, the same class on every send.
    public CannotReturn = (
      ^outer PlatformFactory CannotReturn.
    )

    /// Hands out the kernel's `CannotInstantiate` class to a program.
    ///
    /// @answers the kernel's class `CannotInstantiate`, the same class on every send.
    public CannotInstantiate = (
      ^outer PlatformFactory CannotInstantiate.
    )

    /// Hands out the kernel's `Closure` class to a program.
    ///
    /// @answers the kernel's class `Closure`, the same class on every send.
    public Closure = (
      ^outer PlatformFactory Closure.
    )

    /// Hands out the kernel's `Future` class to a program.
    ///
    /// @answers the kernel's class `Future`, the same class on every send.
    public Future = (
      ^outer PlatformFactory Future.
    )

    /// Hands out the kernel's `Proxy` class to a program.
    ///
    /// @answers the kernel's class `Proxy`, the same class on every send.
    public Proxy = (
      ^outer PlatformFactory Proxy.
    )

    /// Hands out the kernel's abstract collection class, for a program to
    /// subclass.
    ///
    /// @answers the kernel's `Collection` class, the abstract superclass of
    /// `Array`, `List`, `Map` and `Set`, the same class on every send.
    public Collection = (
      ^outer PlatformFactory Collection.
    )

    /// Hands out the kernel's `StringBuilder` class, which a program
    /// instantiates with `new` or `new:` to build a String from pieces.
    ///
    /// @answers the kernel's class `StringBuilder`, the same class on every
    /// send.
    public StringBuilder = (
      ^outer PlatformFactory StringBuilder.
    )

    /// Hands out the kernel's `DataView` class, which a program
    /// instantiates with `on:byteOrder:` a ByteArray or `new:byteOrder:`.
    ///
    /// @answers the kernel's class `DataView`, the same class on every send.
    public DataView = (
      ^outer PlatformFactory DataView.
    )

    /// Hands out the kernel's `WeakArray` class, which a program
    /// instantiates with `new:` for a sequence whose slots do not keep
    /// their objects alive.
    ///
    /// @answers the kernel's class `WeakArray`, the same class on every
    /// send.
    public WeakArray = (
      ^outer PlatformFactory WeakArray.
    )

    /// Hands out the kernel's `Ephemeron` class, which a program
    /// instantiates with `new` for a value and a finalizer kept alive
    /// only while their key is.
    ///
    /// @answers the kernel's class `Ephemeron`, the same class on every
    /// send.
    public Ephemeron = (
      ^outer PlatformFactory Ephemeron.
    )

    /// Hands out the kernel's `WeakMap` class, which a program
    /// instantiates with `new` for a map whose entries last only while
    /// their keys do.
    ///
    /// @answers the kernel's class `WeakMap`, the same class on every send.
    public WeakMap = (
      ^outer PlatformFactory WeakMap.
    )

    /// Runs a full collection: every object that nothing but weak slots
    /// reaches is reclaimed, and those slots read nil before the sender's
    /// next instruction runs.
    ///
    /// An ordinary method, not a forwarder to the mirror: the collection
    /// the kernel's `garbageCollect` asks for is served at the safepoint
    /// of this method's return, so a method of its own must stand between
    /// the program and the leaf.
    ///
    /// @answers the receiver.
    public garbageCollect = (
      kernelModule garbageCollect.
    )
  )

  /// Builds the platform a program is handed: the one public member of
  /// the module, named `build` like every shipped factory's.
  ///
  /// @answers a new `Platform`, what the host hands every program.
  public build = (
    ^Platform new.
  )
)
